silm:instances_papers_04_forge_chapters_02_typing_law_sections_04_sous_observation_role_decomposition_step_5__step_forge_morphism_for_04_sous_observation_role a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The sous position determines Mittens uniquely: two different objects with the same full Hom-profile are isomorphic. This is why the sous position is the Forge's identity-preservation mechanism: as long as the full profile is maintained (neither side collapsed nor conflated), the object is uniquely determined." .
